head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Paper Trail state content replacement review</title><style>body{font:16px/1.65 Arial,sans-serif;color:#202020;max-width:1250px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 20px}h1,h2{text-align:center}a{color:inherit;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:20px}figure{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:12px;margin:0}img{width:100%;height:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:10px;border:1px solid #ccc;text-align:left}details{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:16px;margin:14px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:18px}blockquote{margin:12px 0;padding:14px;background:#f4f4f4;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.warning{border:2px solid #686868;padding:18px}.shots{margin-top:25px}</style>'
parts=[head,'<h1>50 State Content Replacement Review</h1><p>All 50 existing state pages now use the matching content from paper-trail-50-state-bookkeeping-pages-expanded.md. The supplied file is unchanged. Page shells, flags, canonical URLs, service links, fonts, colors, and responsive state layouts are preserved. Informational content, descriptions, and structured data citations were updated. Supplied Markdown links and bare source URLs are clickable. One supplied Utah URL with spaces was encoded for browser use. Narrative word hyphens were replaced with spaces, while URLs, official source names, form numbers, and technical identifiers retain their punctuation.</p>',
 '<div class="warning"><strong>Publication review is pending for every state.</strong> The supplied file explicitly calls for editorial and factual review. Claim corrections have not been silently substituted. Existing noindex,follow metadata and sitemap exclusions remain in place, so these local pages are crawlable but are not approved for Google indexing. Indexing and sitemap inclusion require the remaining claim review and owner approval. No Git actions or publication were performed.</div>',
 '<h2>Verification</h2><p>50 correct state mappings, 50 preserved canonical URLs, 50 preserved flag sets, one H1 per state, 886 paragraphs, and 428 sections. All 1,900 internal links resolve locally. All 150 state page and viewport checks passed at 390, 834, and 1440 pixels without missing images, horizontal overflow, or runtime exceptions. Title and description metadata are unique for each state.</p>',
 '<p>134 unique supplied source URLs checked with read only GET requests: 103 succeeded, one returned 404, and 30 could not be verified due to access or network restrictions. Successful access does not establish factual accuracy. Five supplied paragraphs are repeated verbatim across all 50 states and are flagged for editorial review.</p>',
 '<h2>Primary Review Issues</h2><ul><li>Indiana, New Jersey, and Wyoming have no direct source URLs in the supplied content.</li><li>Connecticut cites OP-210 for a general sales and use tax statement. <a href="https://portal.ct.gov/drs/drs-forms/sales-tax-forms/room-occupancy">Connecticut DRS lists OP-210 as Room Occupancy Tax</a>. It also uses a staging site for a payroll citation.</li><li>Texas annual filing language needs qualification against the <a href="https://comptroller.texas.gov/taxes/franchise/index.php/taxes/franchise/">current Comptroller reporting exceptions</a>.</li><li>West Virginia cites a minimum severance statute while describing another act. Check the scope against <a href="https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-12B-14/">the official code</a>.</li><li>Florida supplied https://floridarevenue.com/rules/Pages/12D-51.001.aspx returned HTTP 404.</li><li>Malformed statutory identifiers, secondary summaries, search snippets, and references to missing numbered sections appear in multiple states. Details follow for each affected state.</li></ul>',
 '<h2>Language Notice and Menu Corrections</h2><p>The centered language notice is now 16 pixels on desktop and iPad and 15 pixels on phones, across all ten languages. Sixty language and viewport checks passed. The reproduced desktop dropdown shifted the header and page down by 89 pixels. Dropdowns now overlay the page on desktop and iPad, with no change to the header or main content position when opened. Initial submenu markup is hidden to avoid a flash before menu initialization. The previously approved phone dropdown behavior remains unchanged.</p>',
 '<h2>Individual State Reviews</h2><p>Each state has been mapped and checked separately. States without automated citation flags still require a full legal fact check before publication. Shared repetition is flagged for every state.</p>']
for row in reviews:
 parts+=['<details id="'+row['state'].lower().replace(' ','-')+'"><summary>'+html.escape(row['state'])+' Bookkeeping, replacement complete, publication review pending</summary><p><a href="../../'+row['page']+'">Open local page</a>, '+str(row['source_count'])+' direct source URLs</p><p>'+html.escape(row['shared_content_note'])+'</p>']
 for flag in row['flags']:
  parts+=['<p><strong>'+html.escape(flag['category'])+'</strong></p><blockquote>'+html.escape(flag['supplied_text'])+'</blockquote>']
  if flag.get('verification_url'):parts+=['<p><a href="'+html.escape(flag['verification_url'],quote=True)+'">Official verification source</a></p>']
 if not row['flags']:parts+=['<p>No specific automated citation or cross reference flag was found. This is not an accuracy approval. Independently verify legal obligations, dates, deadlines, retention periods, and source applicability.</p>']
 if row['source_access']['unverified']:
  parts+=['<p>Source access needs manual review:</p><ul>']
